# Every non-test Go string in cmd and internal that says "relay", with the class a person gave it.
# server = the server (its address, commands, refusals); storage = the switch that lets it keep sealed copies;
# other-feature = a different feature that says the word (only the model pool's own files).
# model-prompt = an instruction to the model using the plain verb ("relay it"), only in internal/session; to be reworded.
# Regenerate with: go test ./internal/wordlaw -run Relay -update   Then read the diff.
# Format: class<TAB>path<TAB>quoted text
model-prompt	internal/session/assignment_tool.go	"Fold a direction the PERSON just gave you into what this task is for. Only for a line that CHANGES THE JOB — a different output format, a different target, a requirement dropped or added — and only citing the direction id that carried it. A fact you were handed (\"the config lives under etc/\"), a question about your approach, and anything another agent relayed are NOT this: use them, answer them, and leave the assignment alone. What you set here is what the checker will judge the finished work against, so state it as an observable condition and keep everything the person did not change."
model-prompt	internal/session/jobs.go	"— this already happened: relay it if it matters, never re-run it and never poll for it."
model-prompt	internal/session/tools_capabilities.go	"A refusal is the person's own machine answering and not an error to work around: relay it exactly as "
model-prompt	internal/session/tools_floor.go	"tell (with item) passes the person's words to that job's main agent, gives it one turn of its own conversation, and answers what it said, for you to relay. Use it only when the person asks in this turn; the turn is charged to the job's budget and is stopped after "
